{
  "mappings": [
    {
      "name": "read: any payment of ours reads complete, for the charge's 5000 XAF",
      "priority": 10,
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "urlPathPattern": "/payments/[0-9a-f-]{36}",
        "headers": {
          "X-Grant": {
            "matches": ".+"
          },
          "Authorization": {
            "matches": ".+"
          }
        }
      },
      "response": {
        "status": 202,
        "headers": {
          "Content-Type": "application/json"
        },
        "body": "{\"code\":202,\"status\":\"Accepted\",\"message\":\"Payment retrieved\",\"transaction\":{\"id\":\"pay.test_{{randomValue length=12 type='ALPHANUMERIC'}}\",\"reference\":\"{{request.pathSegments.[1]}}\",\"amount\":5000,\"currency\":\"XAF\",\"status\":\"complete\"}}"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "why": [
          "openapi.yaml 2.1.0's retrievePayment documents 202 on success, with the payment under",
          "`transaction`. Some API reference pages show `data` instead (RFC-0012 section 10 item 15);",
          "the client follows the specification. The amount and currency are the conformance charge's,",
          "because the adapter refuses a success for any other money (ADR-0031 condition 5)."
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "read: Notch Pay has no record (404 Payment not found)",
      "priority": 1,
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "urlPath": "/payments/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000404",
        "headers": {
          "X-Grant": {
            "matches": ".+"
          },
          "Authorization": {
            "matches": ".+"
          }
        }
      },
      "response": {
        "status": 404,
        "headers": {
          "Content-Type": "application/json"
        },
        "jsonBody": {
          "code": 404,
          "status": "Not Found",
          "message": "Payment not found"
        }
      },
      "metadata": {
        "why": "REF_UNKNOWN. Only Notch Pay's own words are NotFound; any other 404 is Config (RFC-0012 section 3)."
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "read: the rail is down (503)",
      "priority": 1,
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "urlPath": "/payments/00000000-0000-0000-0000-0000000005aa",
        "headers": {
          "X-Grant": {
            "matches": ".+"
          },
          "Authorization": {
            "matches": ".+"
          }
        }
      },
      "response": {
        "status": 503
      },
      "metadata": {
        "why": "REF_UNAVAILABLE. Transport, never a decline."
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "read: slower than the configured deadline",
      "priority": 1,
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "urlPath": "/payments/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000560",
        "headers": {
          "X-Grant": {
            "matches": ".+"
          },
          "Authorization": {
            "matches": ".+"
          }
        }
      },
      "response": {
        "status": 202,
        "headers": {
          "Content-Type": "application/json"
        },
        "body": "{\"code\":202,\"status\":\"Accepted\",\"message\":\"Payment retrieved\",\"transaction\":{\"id\":\"pay.test_{{randomValue length=12 type='ALPHANUMERIC'}}\",\"reference\":\"00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000560\",\"amount\":5000,\"currency\":\"XAF\",\"status\":\"pending\"}}",
        "fixedDelayMilliseconds": 2000
      },
      "metadata": {
        "why": "REF_SLOW. Two orders of magnitude above the suite's SHORT_REQUEST_TIMEOUT, so the case proves the adapter applies ProviderConfig::request_timeout per request (Client::with_request_timeout)."
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "read: a body far larger than any answer Notch Pay documents",
      "priority": 1,
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "urlPath": "/payments/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000b16",
        "headers": {
          "X-Grant": {
            "matches": ".+"
          },
          "Authorization": {
            "matches": ".+"
          }
        }
      },
      "response": {
        "status": 202,
        "headers": {
          "Content-Type": "application/json"
        },
        "body": "{\"code\":202,\"transaction\":{\"id\":\"pay.test_0b16\",\"reference\":\"00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000b16\",\"amount\":5000,\"currency\":\"XAF\",\"status\":\"complete\"},\"padding\":\"{{randomValue length=300000 type='ALPHANUMERIC'}}\"}"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "why": "REF_HUGE. A valid complete read padded past MAX_RAIL_BODY_BYTES (256 KiB), so without the bound the adapter would answer Succeeded."
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "decline: failed",
      "priority": 1,
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "urlPath": "/payments/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000f01",
        "headers": {
          "X-Grant": {
            "matches": ".+"
          },
          "Authorization": {
            "matches": ".+"
          }
        }
      },
      "response": {
        "status": 202,
        "headers": {
          "Content-Type": "application/json"
        },
        "body": "{\"code\":202,\"status\":\"Accepted\",\"message\":\"Payment retrieved\",\"transaction\":{\"id\":\"pay.test_{{randomValue length=12 type='ALPHANUMERIC'}}\",\"reference\":\"00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000f01\",\"amount\":5000,\"currency\":\"XAF\",\"status\":\"failed\"}}"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "why": "Notch Pay's read names no reason (RFC-0012 section 4): failed is provider_error until the sandbox shows otherwise."
      }
    },
    {
